<header><p class="enc-kicker">Event</p><h1 class="enc-title">Parliament of Ravennika</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1209</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Parliament of Ravennika was an assembly held in May 1209 at Ravennika, in central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greece">Greece</a>, by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/latin">Latin</a> Emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henry-of-flanders">Henry of Flanders</a>. The lords of Frankish Greece, among them <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/geoffrey-i-of-villehardouin">Geoffrey I of Villehardouin</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/achaea">Achaea</a>, recognised the emperor's suzerainty, and a second meeting in 1210 regulated the position of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/latin-christendom">Latin Church</a>.</p></div>
